{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter004-001","severity":"P2","label":"Apply acceptance is workflow-gated rather than fully enforced by the engine. The engine automatically queues take-release files for update/new units, and align pre-fills adopt-release for unchanged files in customized units. The routed workflows require per-file answers and startup approval for the exact dry-run plan, but a direct engine invocation can consume those defaults without an operator calling decide for each file.","iteration":4,"sources":[".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs",".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-align.yaml",".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-apply.yaml"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter004-002","severity":"P2","label":"A recorded base without a tree fingerprint is accepted as recorded because baseForUnit allows !record.tree; buildReport then does not list that base for record-base remediation. This weakens provenance for legacy or edited base records. A stale-tag data-loss outcome was not demonstrated.","iteration":4,"sources":[".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs"]}
{"type":"invariant","id":"inv-iter004-001","label":"align writes evidence, proposals, plan.json and decisions.json under runDir; its test confirms checkout status contains only run-directory changes, while --dry-run creates no run directory.","iteration":4}
{"type":"observation","id":"obs-iter004-001","label":"New base records carry release plus a per-unit tree fingerprint; file plans/evidence carry base, local and release blob ids and modes. Merge/use-proposal decisions bind proposalSha256 and apply rechecks it.","iteration":4}
{"type":"observation","id":"obs-iter004-002","label":"No silent overwrite path was proven for the routed apply path: local/release blobs are checked against the plan, targets are checked for staged or unstaged changes before and under the lock, and rollback skips paths whose current state differs from the applied state. Generated artifacts are left for named generator follow-ups; authored graph-metadata fields outside derived remain authored.","iteration":4}
